abstract: "This study investigates the effects of napping and meditation on memory consolidation, examining whether meditation, as a state of wakefulness with sleep-like characteristics, can facilitate memory consolidation similar to sleep. The research compares declarative and non-declarative memory performance across three conditions: meditation, napping, and wakefulness, using Bayesian statistical analysis and EEG spectral analysis."
